---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'June 10, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Lagos Privacy Policy — how we handle your data, audio, and personal information."
>
  <article class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-3" style="color: var(--color-text);">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm mb-10" style="color: var(--color-text-muted);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Lagos ("we", "our", "the app") is a macOS voice dictation application. We take your privacy seriously, especially because Lagos processes audio. This policy explains what data we collect, how we use it, and your choices.
        </p>

        <h2>Audio and Transcription</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Audio is never stored on disk.</strong> When you hold your shortcut to record, audio is captured in memory only. It is sent to the transcription engine you have selected and then immediately discarded.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Apple Speech:</strong> Audio is processed by macOS Speech Recognition. Apple's privacy policy applies. No audio leaves your device through Lagos.</li>
          <li><strong>WhisperKit:</strong> Audio is processed entirely on-device using Core ML. Nothing is ever sent to a server.</li>
          <li><strong>Parakeet (Beta):</strong> Audio is processed entirely on-device via FluidAudio/Core ML. Nothing is ever sent to a server.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Every engine Lagos ships today is on-device. If optional cloud engines (e.g. bring-your-own-key providers) ship in the future, they will be strictly opt-in, clearly labeled, and this policy will be updated first.
        </p>

        <h2>Transcription History</h2>
        <p>
          Transcribed text is saved locally to a SQLite database at <code>~/Library/Application Support/Lagos/history.db</code> on your device. This data never leaves your device unless you export it manually. You can delete your history at any time from Lagos settings.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics &amp; Crash Reports</h2>
        <p>
          Lagos collects anonymous usage analytics and crash reports via Firebase (Analytics and Crashlytics) to understand which features are used and to fix bugs. This is <strong>on by default and disclosed during onboarding</strong>, with a single switch to turn it off: <strong>Settings → Privacy → "Send anonymous usage data"</strong>. This data is:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Anonymous — identified only by a random UUID, never linked to your identity, Apple ID, or any account</li>
          <li>Limited to events like "recording started", "engine changed", "settings opened", plus crash stack traces</li>
          <li><strong>Never</strong> your audio, and <strong>never</strong> the content of your transcriptions</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          In-app feedback you choose to submit (Settings → Feedback) is sent to our database along with basic diagnostic info (app version, anonymized device ID) so we can act on it.
        </p>

        <h2>Website</h2>
        <p>
          This website (trylagos.app) runs no analytics or tracking scripts. Our hosting provider (Vercel) keeps standard, short-lived server access logs. If you choose to enter your email for release updates, it is stored with our email provider (Resend) solely to send you those updates — unsubscribe anytime, and we never sell or share it.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or data deletion requests, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@ragtaglabs.dev">support@ragtaglabs.dev</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as the app evolves. Material changes will be announced via the in-app update notes or blog.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
